## How Prompt Cache / Slot Reuse Works

The system has **two layers** of prompt reuse:

### 1. Slot-level LCP selection (in `get_available_slot`, `server-context.cpp:1586`)

When a new task arrives, the server first tries to find a **slot whose cached prompt shares a long common prefix** with the incoming task's tokens:

```cpp
// fraction of the Longest Common Prefix length with respect to the input prompt length
const float sim_cur = float(tokens.get_common_prefix(task.tokens)) / task.tokens.size();

// select the current slot if the criteria match
if (sim_cur > sim_best && sim_cur > slot_prompt_similarity) {
    sim_best = sim_cur;
    ret = &slot;
}
```

The threshold is `slot_prompt_similarity` (default `0.0`, meaning disabled; set via `--cache-prompt-similarity` or similar). If no slot exceeds the similarity threshold, the **LRU slot** is chosen instead.

If the chosen slot would **lose a large portion of its context** (`f_keep < 0.5f`), its current prompt is **saved into the global prompt cache** before being overwritten:

```cpp
if (f_keep < 0.5f) {
    update_cache = true;
}
...
if (update_cache) {
    ret->prompt_save(*prompt_cache);
    if (!ret->prompt_load(*prompt_cache, task.tokens)) {
        ret->prompt_clear(false);
    }
    prompt_cache->update();
}
```

### 2. Global prompt cache (`server_prompt_cache`, `server-task.cpp:1601`)

The cache is a `std::list<server_prompt>` where each entry holds:
- `tokens` — the token sequence
- `data` — serialized llama KV-cache state (main + draft contexts)
- `checkpoints` — checkpoint offsets for context trimming

**`alloc()`** (`server-task.cpp:1623`) does two prefix checks:

```cpp
// first check if the current state is contained fully in the cache
for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
    const int cur_lcp_len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
    if (cur_lcp_len == (int) prompt.tokens.size()) {
        SRV_TRC("%s", " - prompt is already in the cache, skipping\n");
        return nullptr;  // exact match, no need to save
    }
}

// next, remove any cached prompts that are fully contained in the current prompt
for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end();) {
    const int len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
    if (len == (int) it->tokens.size()) {
        SRV_TRC(" - removing obsolete cached prompt with length %d\n", len);
        it = states.erase(it);
    } else {
        ++it;
    }
}
```

**`load()`** (`server-task.cpp:1678`) picks the **best cached prompt** by maximizing both:
- `f_keep = lcp / cached_prompt_size` — fraction of the cached prompt that is preserved
- `sim = lcp / new_prompt_size` — fraction of the new prompt covered by the cached prefix

```cpp
const int lcp_best = prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

float f_keep_best = prompt.tokens.size() > 0 ? float(lcp_best) / prompt.tokens.size() : -1.0f;
float sim_best    = float(lcp_best) / tokens_new.size();

for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
    const int lcp_cur = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);
    const float f_keep_cur = float(lcp_cur) / it->tokens.size();
    const float sim_cur    = float(lcp_cur) / tokens_new.size();

    // don't trash large prompts
    if (f_keep_cur < 0.25f) {
        continue;
    }

    if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur) {
        f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
        sim_best    = sim_cur;
        it_best = it;
    }
}
```

If a better match is found, the KV-cache state is restored via `llama_state_seq_set_data_ext()` and the entry is **moved** into the slot:

```cpp
prompt = std::move(*it_best);
states.erase(it_best);
```

### 3. The actual common-prefix computation (`server-common.cpp:471`)

```cpp
size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        return max_idx;
    }

    // multimodal-aware: LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL markers represent media chunks;
    // match by chunk id + token count rather than individual tokens
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai = tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
