// select the current slot if the criteria match
if (sim_cur > sim_best && sim_cur > slot_prompt_similarity) {
    sim_best = sim_cur;
    ret = &slot;
}
```

The threshold is `slot_prompt_similarity` (default 0.0 = disabled). If no slot passes, it falls back to **LRU** (least-recently-used) slot selection.

### 2. Common Prefix Matching (`get_common_prefix` in `server-common.cpp`)

The actual prefix comparison is a linear scan over token vectors:

```cpp
size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        return max_idx;
    }

    // multimodal path: when both sides hit LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL, compare media chunk IDs
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai = tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
            const auto & a_chunk = find_chunk(i);
            const auto & b_chunk = b.find_chunk(i);
            const std::string id_ai = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(a_chunk.get());
            const std::string id_bi = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(b_chunk.get());
            if (id_ai == id_bi && n_tok_a == n_tok_b) {
                i += n_tok_a - 1; // skip the whole media chunk
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        if (ai == bi) continue;
        return i;
    }
    return max_idx;
}
```

For plain text, it's a simple token-by-token equality check. For multimodal prompts, `LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL` markers represent media chunks, and matching requires the **chunk ID** and **token count** to be identical — so the same image/video file reused across requests will match.

### 3. Cache Save/Load (`server_prompt_cache` in `server-task.cpp`)

When a slot is selected but its cached prompt would lose too much context (`f_keep < 0.5`), the slot's current KV state is **saved** into the cache:

```cpp
