## How prompt cache / slot reuse works

The prompt cache system has three interacting layers:

### 1. Slot selection via LCP similarity (`get_available_slot`, server-context.cpp:1586)

When a new request arrives, the server tries to find a **slot** whose cached prompt shares a long common prefix with the incoming task:

```cpp
server_slot * get_available_slot(const server_task & task) {
    // ...
    if (slot_prompt_similarity != 0.0f) {
        float sim_best = 0;
        for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
            if (slot.is_processing()) continue;
            const auto & tokens = slot.prompt.tokens;
            if (tokens.empty()) continue;

            // fraction of the Longest Common Prefix length with respect to the input prompt length
            const float sim_cur = float(tokens.get_common_prefix(task.tokens)) / task.tokens.size();

            if (sim_cur > sim_best && sim_cur > slot_prompt_similarity) {
                sim_best = sim_cur;
                ret = &slot;
            }
        }

        if (ret != nullptr) {
            const float f_keep = (sim_best*task.tokens.size()) / ret->prompt.tokens.size();
            // if we are about to lose a large portion of the existing context - save it in the prompt cache
            if (f_keep < 0.5f) {
                update_cache = true;
            }
        }
    }
    // ...
}
```

`slot_prompt_similarity` is set from `--slot-prompt-similarity` (default 0.1). If no slot meets the threshold, the server falls back to **LRU slot selection** and still triggers a cache update.

### 2. The `get_common_prefix` implementation (server-common.cpp:471)

This is the core token-level LCP matching:

```cpp
size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        return max_idx;
    }

    // multimodal-aware: LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL represents media chunks
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai = tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
            const auto & a_chunk = find_chunk(i);
            const auto & b_chunk = b.find_chunk(i);

            const std::string id_ai = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(a_chunk.get());
            const std::string id_bi = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(b_chunk.get());

            const size_t n_tok_a = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(a_chunk.get());
            const size_t n_tok_b = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(b_chunk.get());

            if (id_ai == id_bi && n_tok_a == n_tok_b) {
                i += n_tok_a - 1; // skip the whole media chunk
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }

        if (ai == bi) continue;
        return i;
    }
    return max_idx;
}
```

For plain text it's a simple token-by-token comparison. For multimodal prompts, `LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL` tokens act as placeholders for media chunks; matching requires the chunk ID and token count to be identical, then the loop skips the entire chunk.

### 3. Cache save/load with two metrics (`server_prompt_cache::alloc` and `load`, server-task.cpp:1623–1752)

When a slot is selected but its cached prompt would be mostly discarded (`f_keep < 0.5`), the slot's current prompt is **saved** to the cache via `prompt_save()` → `alloc()`:

```cpp
server_prompt * server_prompt_cache::alloc(const server_prompt & prompt, size_t state_size_tgt, size_t state_size_dft) {
    // skip if already fully in cache
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int cur_lcp_len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
        if (cur_lcp_len == (int) prompt.tokens.size()) {
            return nullptr; // already cached
        }
    }

    // remove cached prompts fully contained in the new one
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end();) {
        const int len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
        if (len == (int) it->tokens.size()) {
            it = states.erase(it);
        } else {
            ++it;
        }
    }

    // allocate KV state buffers and push to cache
    states.push_back({prompt.tokens.clone(), {state_data_tgt, state_data_dft}, prompt.checkpoints});
    return &states.back();
}
```

When loading a cached prompt for a new request, `load()` picks the **best** cached entry using two metrics:

```cpp
bool server_prompt_cache::load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tokens_new, ...) {
    const int lcp_best = prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

    float f_keep_best = prompt.tokens.size() > 0 ? float(lcp_best) / prompt.tokens.size() : -1.0f;
    float sim_best    = float(lcp_best) / tokens_new.size();

    auto it_best = states.end();

    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int lcp_cur = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);
        const float f_keep_cur = float(lcp_cur) / it->tokens.size();
        const float sim_cur    = float(lcp_cur) / tokens_new.size();

        // don't trash large prompts
        if (f_keep_cur < 0.25f) continue;

        if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur) {
            f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
            sim_best    = sim_cur;
            it_best = it;
        }
    }

    if (it_best != states.end()) {
        // restore llama_state_seq into ctx_tgt (and ctx_dft for speculative)
        llama_state_seq_set_data_ext(ctx_tgt, data.data(), size, id_slot, 0);
        prompt = std::move(*it_best);
        states.erase(it_best);
    }
    return true;
}
```

- **`f_keep`** = LCP / cached_prompt_length — how much of the cached prompt is preserved. Entries with `f_keep < 0.25` are rejected (too much context lost).
- **`sim`** = LCP / new_prompt_length — how much of the new prompt is covered.

Both must improve over the current slot's state for a cache hit to be chosen.

### 4. Eviction (`update()`, server-task.cpp:1753)

The cache is bounded by `--cache-ram` (MiB) and a token limit. `update()` evicts the **oldest** entries (front of the `std::list`) until both limits are satisfied, dynamically adjusting the token limit based on average bytes-per-token.

---

**Summary of the flow:**

1. `get_available_slot()` scans slots for LCP similarity ≥ `slot_prompt_similarity`.
2. If a slot's cached prompt would be mostly overwritten (`f_keep < 0.5`), it's saved to the global `server_prompt_cache` before being cleared.
3. `prompt_load()` searches the cache for a better-matching entry using the `f_keep`/`sim` dual metric, restores KV state via `llama_state_seq_set_data_ext`, and replaces the slot's prompt.
4. `prompt_cache.update()` evicts oldest entries if size/token limits are exceeded.

